+  "effort-routing-1": {
+   "id": "effort-routing-1",
+   "title": "High effort's main gain, the USD 1,524m scheduled-interest figure, came from one source search in high's CP-2. No instruction asks for it.",
+   "measured_cost": "No module in the medium run ever saw 1,524 in a tool result. In the high run, CP-2 searched the source 18 times (medium: 5), including for 'Scheduled interest payments', and found it on 10-K p.64. CP-2A, CP-2G and CP-6 then received it in CP-2's handoff and confirmed it. High's CP-1A also read p.64 but did not use the figure. The comparison credits it with high's gains in CP-2, CP-2A, CP-6 and part of CP-3. Running CP-2, CP-2A, CP-3 and CP-6 at high cost +USD 0.17, +0.19, +0.17 and +0.27 per run.",
+   "cause": "The instructions sent to CP-1, CP-2, CP-2A and CP-2G never mention contractual obligations or scheduled or forward interest (grep: 0 hits in each). CP-2A's stress block (cpos_launch.py:1779-1789) anchors the interest shock only to 'a disclosed rate exposure'. So medium's 2.5-10% shock was a legitimate reading of the instruction. Whether a module finds the forward schedule depends on how much it happens to search.",
+   "proposal": "Make it an instruction, not a matter of effort. (a) In CP-1's instructions, ask for a row with next-year scheduled interest payments from the contractual-obligations table, where the filing discloses one, or 'Not supplied: <reason>'. (b) Add one sentence to STRESS_BLOCK: where a forward interest schedule is stated, anchor the cash-interest increase to its step-up over base-period cash interest, or say why not.",
+   "estimated_saving": "Not a direct saving. It makes the gain independent of effort, which is the precondition for keeping CP-3 and CP-6 at medium (\u2212USD 0.44 per run against the balanced map, spliced from calls.jsonl) and possibly CP-2A (\u22120.19). Adding the row costs about 1 extra search per run (unmeasured, under USD 0.02).",
+   "quality_risk": "Low, because it adds evidence. The risk is a module copying a schedule that rests on variable-rate assumptions without that limitation. The row's Basis must carry the issuer's rate assumptions, as high's CP-2 did (5.6-6.5%).",
+   "test_before_adoption": "Answer key frozen from the 10-K before the rerun: the less-than-1-year scheduled interest is 1,524, and CP-2A's k is tied to 1,524/1,158. Rerun TDG all-medium with (a) and (b). Pass if CP-1 prints 1,524 with its rate assumptions, CP-2 states 4,173/1,524 = 2.74x, and CP-2A's interest shock cites the step-up. Repeat on one issuer whose filing has no contractual-obligations table and check that the row reads 'Not supplied'.",
+   "evidence": "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ericguei-Documents-RBOT-HTML--claude-worktrees-do-nothing-77300f/80869fa7-1d01-46dd-969b-09d1c36c5045/scratchpad/opt-review/effort_1524_trace.py, /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ericguei-Documents-RBOT-HTML--claude-worktrees-do-nothing-77300f/80869fa7-1d01-46dd-969b-09d1c36c5045/scratchpad/opt-review/effort_queries.py, /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ericguei-Documents-RBOT-HTML--claude-worktrees-do-nothing-77300f/80869fa7-1d01-46dd-969b-09d1c36c5045/scratchpad/opt-review/effort_map_projection.py; /Users/ericguei/Documents/RBOT-HTML/.claude/worktrees/do-nothing-77300f/src/deploy_workflow/owners/cpos_launch.py:1779-1789; high run CP-2A handoff line 160.",
+   "confidence": "profile-attributed"
+  },
+  "effort-routing-2": {
+   "id": "effort-routing-2",
+   "title": "Medium CP-2G withheld the forecast because medium CP-1 broke an existing instruction that no check enforces. This was not an effort effect.",
+   "measured_cost": "Medium CP-2G published no forecast: its debt operand was null with the reason 'Total carrying debt is stated only in Financial foundation's calculation table'. Per the comparison, that weakened CP-3 and CP-8 and was one of CP-5's 4 Material issues. Fixing it with high effort costs +USD 0.36 per run in CP-2G (1.88x, the highest ratio: 20 calls vs 8, 139 calculate calls vs 14).",
+   "cause": "CP-1's instructions already say (cpos_launch.py:1946-1950): 'Print every balance the forecast needs (total debt, cash, undrawn committed facilities) as a row of a table whose columns are those period headers.' Medium CP-1 printed 24,880 only in its calculation table, plus principal 25,068 in Net debt data. High CP-1 printed a 'Total debt carrying amount' row under FY2024. CP-2G's instruction (cpos_launch.py:1975-1977 and the CP-2G copy) forbids reading from one-row-per-period tables, so medium CP-2G followed its rule correctly. No acceptance check for CP-1 tests the balance rows: the layer-1 operand validation in cpos_forecast.py only runs when CP-2G is absent (cpos_launch.py:2546).",
+   "proposal": "Add a check to CP-1's acceptance whenever a forecast is wanted (the same condition as PERIOD_TABLE_BLOCK, cpos_launch.py:2545). Reject a draft that has no row under a period column for total debt, cash and undrawn committed facilities, unless that row reads 'Not supplied: <reason>'. Name the missing row in the rejection message. Keep CP-2G at medium, as the balanced map already does.",
+   "estimated_saving": "Keeps CP-2G at medium (avoids +USD 0.36 per run) while removing the main downstream defect of medium. A rejection costs about 1 extra CP-1 write when it fires (about USD 0.04-0.06, from CP-1's per-call cost in calls.jsonl).",
+   "quality_risk": "A strict check could push CP-1 to print a principal figure as 'total debt' just to pass. The rule must accept 'Not supplied: <reason>' and must not prescribe carrying or principal. The basis cell keeps that distinction.",
+   "test_before_adoption": "Write a failing test first: feed medium CP-1's accepted handoff (run tdg-full-copilot-sol-001-resume) to the new check and expect a rejection that names total debt. Feed high CP-1's handoff and expect a pass. Then run an all-medium TDG rerun and check that CP-2G publishes base and downside paths, recomputed against the 10-K.",
+   "evidence": "/Users/ericguei/Documents/RBOT-HTML/.claude/worktrees/do-nothing-77300f/src/deploy_workflow/owners/cpos_launch.py:1936-1951, 1975-1977, 2543-2546; medium CP-2G handoff lines 244 and 274; high CP-1 handoff line 36; /Users/ericguei/Documents/RBOT-HTML/.claude/worktrees/do-nothing-77300f/src/deploy_workflow/owners/cpos_forecast.py:286-330; /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ericguei-Documents-RBOT-HTML--claude-worktrees-do-nothing-77300f/80869fa7-1d01-46dd-969b-09d1c36c5045/scratchpad/opt-review/effort_queries.py",
