+   "title": "Medium's CP-1 maturity 'conflict' and CP-DR's 'post-cutoff' exclusion are instruction gaps that one sentence each would close at medium cost.",
+   "measured_cost": "Running CP-1 at high costs +USD 0.21 per run and CP-DR at high +0.16. Medium CP-1 called the November 2027 notes a data conflict (handoff lines 169, 277, 329, 338) and showed 93, not 580, for FY2025 maturities. CP-DR then made the conflict a research target. Medium CP-DR excluded the 10-K as 'signed after the research cutoff' (CP-DR handoff lines 32 and 79), although no cutoff was set. Both runs' CP-0 noted the late signature date, but only medium's CP-DR treated it as an exclusion.",
+   "cause": "The debt-maturities chart rule (cpos_launch.py:606) has no rule placing maturities in the fiscal year that contains them, and none that includes short-term securitization due in the year. The fiscal-year sentence in PERIOD_TABLE_BLOCK (cpos_launch.py:1941-1942) covers period headers only. CP-DR's head states only 'as of 2024-09-30', and its method lists a `freshness` cut-off field (CP-DR instructions line 329), which medium read as a cutoff.",
+   "proposal": "(a) Add to the debt-maturities chart rule: a Period is the issuer's fiscal year; place each maturity in the fiscal year that contains its date (15 November 2027 is FY2028 for a 30 September year-end); include short-term borrowings due in the year, such as securitization, and say so in Basis. (b) Add to CP-DR's head: the as-of date is the financial measurement date; filings that report periods ending on or before it are in scope whatever their signature date; no information cutoff applies unless the context sets one. Keep CP-1 and CP-DR at medium, as BALANCED_HIGH_MODULES already does.",
+   "estimated_saving": "Avoids moving CP-1 and CP-DR to high (USD 0.37 per run, spliced) to fix two errors that travelled downstream. Roughly 100 extra instruction tokens, under USD 0.001 per run.",
+   "quality_risk": "(a) could force securitization into a schedule where the issuer reports it separately. Basis must state the inclusion, and the issuer's own schedule stays visible. (b) must not erase CP-0's correct limitation that this is a fiscal-period retrospective, not a reconstruction of what was public on that date.",
+   "test_before_adoption": "Answer key from the 10-K: the 2027 notes fall in FY2028; FY2025 maturities are 580 including the 487 securitization. Rerun CP-1 and CP-DR at medium on TDG and check both; check that CP-DR uses the 10-K and keeps the retrospective limitation. Add one calendar-year issuer to show (a) does not move its maturities.",
+   "evidence": "/Users/ericguei/Documents/RBOT-HTML/.claude/worktrees/do-nothing-77300f/src/deploy_workflow/owners/cpos_launch.py:606, 1936-1942, 2872-2886; medium run instructions/CP-1.md:42 and instructions/CP-DR.md:1, 14, 329; medium deliveries CP-1.md and CP-DR.md (lines above); /Users/ericguei/Documents/RBOT-HTML/.claude/worktrees/do-nothing-77300f/runs/tdg-mixed-effort-comparison.md (two earlier medium CP-1 runs were adequate)",
