+   "quality_risk": "CP-3 (credit view) and CP-6 (committee challenge) are the reader's front page. If medium CP-3 or CP-6 drops the 2.74x coverage point or the funding-gap quantification, even with a high-effort CP-2 upstream, the reader loses the decisive evidence.",
+   "test_before_adoption": "Run-to-run noise is unknown, and the earlier mixed comparison showed CP-0 varying as much between two medium runs as between efforts. Run at least 3 runs per arm (balanced default vs proposed map), with findings 1-3 adopted in both arms, on TDG and on at least one other issuer that has executed documents (so CP-4 is not Blocked) and a different fiscal year-end. That is about 12 runs at roughly USD 9-10 each, about USD 115, each run within the USD 20 cap. Score against a frozen checklist written before the runs: 2.74x present in CP-2, CP-3 and CP-6; forecast published; funding gap quantified; Material issues raised by CP-5. Adopt only if the proposed arm matches the balanced arm on every item in at least 2 of 3 runs per issuer.",
